CLASS:: MP3Short
SUMMARY:: Trim the three short windows independently
CATEGORIES:: UGens>MPEG Audio
RELATED:: Guides/MPEGAudio, Classes/MP3Clock, Classes/MP3Pack

DESCRIPTION::
Apply dB trims to MP3 short windows. Long-window bands pass through.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: ar
Use the resulting bank as the frame’s attenuation field.

ARGUMENT:: attenuation
Effective MP3 attenuation, one scalar or one signal per hybrid band.

ARGUMENT:: window
Window code per channel. Codes 2, 4 and 5 select short or mixed windows.

ARGUMENT:: row
Current spectral row from 0 through 17, usually the first output of MP3Clock.

ARGUMENT:: trims
Three dB values, one per short window. Six values allow separate stereo trims. Negative values attenuate.

ARGUMENT:: channels
One or two output channels. Supply an integer when compiling the SynthDef.

RETURNS:: 32 or 64 audio-rate attenuation signals.
